        "title": "OpenAI launches ChatGPT Wallet, enabling ‘dot’ agents to make purchases",
        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/11/13/openai-launches-chatgpt-wallet-enabling-dot-agents-to-make-purchases/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/06/chatgpt-green.webp?w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">OpenAI is launching ChatGPT Wallet, which it says is “setting a new bar for secure payments by agents.”</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">ChatGPT Wallet works with OpenAI’s “dots” agent feature and includes a partnership with American Express, MasterCard, and Visa. Here’s how it works.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"apps,chatgpt,openai\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1079396\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/11/13/openai-launches-chatgpt-wallet-enabling-dot-agents-to-make-purchases/#more-1079396\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
