        "url": "https://www.oreilly.com/radar/why-git-needs-help-moving-from-files-to-systems-for-source-control/",
        "content_text": "The shift to agentic reality When Git was designed in 2005, Linus Torvalds solved a brilliant problem for humans collaborating over terminal windows by trading line-by-line diffs. Fast-forward to 2026: Autonomous coding agents don’t think in flat text files or line breaks. They reason across syntax trees, execution traces, call graphs, and type constraints. In [&#8230;]",
